ralph/codex-output/iteration-000021-20260518-183721.log:1009:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, OpenAPI-conformance instance (BE-0382 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_openapi_conformance_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/openapi/openapi_conformance_test.go + SECURITY.md "## OpenAPI Schema Conformance Tests" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: OpenAPI schema conformance tests (BE-0382)" subsection; FOURTH worked instance of the BE-0379/BE-0380/BE-0381 verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test mega-pattern). Two BE-0382-specific extensions to the template: (1) `-RUN-FILTER PREFIX CONTRACT` — when the PRD already carries a `-run TestXxx ./...` filter for the suite (BE-0382 inherited `-run TestOpenAPI ./...` from the PRD's verificationLoop array unchanged; that filter previously matched zero tests because the existing openapi tests are `TestBuild…` / `TestOperation…` not `TestOpenAPI…`), the canonical-funcs entries MUST satisfy the `-run` filter prefix or the named gate silently matches zero tests. The static test pins this with a dedicated `<subject>PrefixLocksTheRunFilterContract` analyzer subtest that walks the canonical-funcs list and asserts every entry begins with `func TestOpenAPI` (or whatever the suite's filter prefix is). Forward-applicable to BE-0383 (`-run TestPolicyMatrix`), BE-0384 (`-run TestQuotaConcurrency`), and BE-0386 (`-run TestFakeDokploy`); NOT applicable to BE-0385 (no `-run` filter — package-level only). When picking up such a sibling story FIRST check whether the PRD's `-run` filter currently matches any test (`go test -run <PrefixPattern> ./...` shows `no tests to run` everywhere) — if so, the story MUST add tests that satisfy the prefix, not just wire the dedicated step. (2) `VALUE-TYPE STRUCT FIELD SHAPE` — when the canonical conformance test reads a struct field that's a value type (not a pointer), the tes