ralph/codex-output/iteration-000004-20260518-155115.log:1226:- Repository tenant-isolation tests for a **TABLE WHOSE *_repository.go, PRIMARY *_test.go AND *_repository_invariants_test.go ALREADY EXIST FROM A PRIOR (NON-PRD) SUBSYSTEM STORY + BE-046x INVARIANTS STORY** -- i.e. the tenant-isolation PRD story follows the same gap-fill pattern as the invariants story did (BE-0462 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/job_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go for provisioning_jobs). Five load-bearing differences from a first-story-for-table tenant-isolation vertical (BE-0458 deployments, BE-0456 quota_reservations, etc.): (a) NO migration is added -- the table was already exercised by both the subsystem story AND the BE-046x invariants story; (b) the rawXxxRow/loadXxxRowByID/countXxxRowsForOrg/mintXxxID/xxxTxRollbackSentinel helpers ALREADY EXIST in the invariants_test file in the SAME package store_test -- grep BEFORE writing and REUSE verbatim; (c) the lightweight cross-tenant smoke tests in the subsystem _test.go are kept (do NOT delete them) and this file is a GAP-FILL against the canonical *_tenant_isolation_test.go template (deployment_tenant_isolation_test.go is the closest template), adding the byte-identity bystander proofs / no-leak substring checks / per-tenant COUNT(*) invariance / cascade-tenant-scope proofs the smoke tests deliberately did not pin; (d) helpers introduced here MUST carry the per-file suffix (`Job`, `Dep`, `QR`, ...) and ARE distinct from the rawXxxRow/loadXxxRowByID family already exported by the invariants file (those are in the same package); the new ones to add are timePtrEqualXxx, fmtTimePtrXxx, strPtrEqualXxx, fmtStrPtrXxx (only if the table has nullable *string columns), assertXxxByteIdentical, twoTenantXxxFixture+seedTwoTenantXxxFixture, plus one or two opinionated `seedYyyXxx` wrappers (e.g. seedQueuedJob/seedRunningJob); (e) when the table has NO `version` column (provisioning_jobs is the canonical example, vs deployments/projects/services which DO have one), the `assertXxxByteIdentical` MUST NOT compare a version column and the file header MUST call out `updated_at` as the SOLE trigger-managed drift anchor (the BEFORE UPDATE set_updated_at trigger is the load-bearing anchor; a missing organization_id predicate would surface as updated_at drift even when every other column happened to look right). Mandatory test shape (the 8 tests this file lands, adapted from BE-0458): Insert(orgA)DoesNotTouchOrgB (byte-identity over queued + running-with-live-lease + idempotency-collide bystanders), Insert(orgA)DoesNotChangeOrgBRowCount, InsertSameIdempotencyKeyInTwoTenantsBothPersist (positive direction + per-tenant FindByIdempotencyKey round-trip), GetCrossTenantReturnsNotFoundAndDoesNotEcho (typed apierr.NotFound + substring no-leak on idempotency_key/request_id/correlation_id/project_id), FindByIdempotencyKeyCrossTenantDoesNotLeak (returns (zero, false, nil) + zero-value field-by-field no-leak), <StateMutation>CrossTenantLeavesOrgABystandersByteIdentical (the table's single mutating surface attempted by orgB on orgA's id -- Cancel for deployments, Transition(..., cancelled, mut) for jobs -- MUST surface as apierr.NotFound NOT Conflict, because the FOR UPDATE SELECT under (organization_id, id) returns ErrNoRows BEFORE the state-machine validator runs; bystanders include the named target + queued sibling + running sibling carrying a live lease), ListByOrganizationCrossTenantReturnsEmptyAndDoesNotLeakTotal (empty slice + side-effect-free read + per-tenant COUNT(*) invariance), OrganizationDeleteCascadeIsTenantScoped (orgA deletion cascades only to orgA's rows; orgB rows survive byte-identical -- include a row carrying a live lease to anchor lease_owner/lease_deadline/started_at). Always document in the file header what the file DELIBERATELY DELEGATES (composite-FK cross-tenant-parent path pinned by invariants story, closed-set / lifecycle CHECKs / state-machine matrix / lease bookkeeping / claimer pinned by subsystem story, redactor + payload marshalling pinned by internal_test) so a future reader does not mistake the omission for a coverage gap. When the table's worker-side claimer is INTENTIONALLY NOT tenant-scoped (e.g. ClaimNext SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED across all tenants), call it out explicitly in the header rationale. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation story whose table follows the (subsystem-tests + invariants-tests + table-has-no-version-column) shape (e.g. future job_attempts / dokploy_refs if their repos land before their PRD stories).
ralph/codex-output/iteration-000004-20260518-155115.log:1281:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, OpenAPI-conformance instance (BE-0382 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_openapi_conformance_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/openapi/openapi_conformance_test.go + SECURITY.md "## OpenAPI Schema Conformance Tests" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: OpenAPI schema conformance tests (BE-0382)" subsection; FOURTH worked instance of the BE-0379/BE-0380/BE-0381 verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test mega-pattern). Two BE-0382-specific extensions to the template: (1) `-RUN-FILTER PREFIX CONTRACT` — when the PRD already carries a `-run TestXxx ./...` filter for the suite (BE-0382 inherited `-run TestOpenAPI ./...` from the PRD's verificationLoop array unchanged; that filter previously matched zero tests because the existing openapi tests are `TestBuild…` / `TestOperation…` not `TestOpenAPI…`), the canonical-funcs entries MUST satisfy the `-run` filter prefix or the named gate silently matches zero tests. The static test pins this with a dedicated `<subject>PrefixLocksTheRunFilterContract` analyzer subtest that walks the canonical-funcs list and asserts every entry begins with `func TestOpenAPI` (or whatever the suite's filter prefix is). Forward-applicable to BE-0383 (`-run TestPolicyMatrix`), BE-0384 (`-run TestQuotaConcurrency`), and BE-0386 (`-run TestFakeDokploy`); NOT applicable to BE-0385 (no `-run` filter — package-level only). When picking up such a sibling story FIRST check whether the PRD's `-run` filter currently matches any test (`go test -run <PrefixPattern> ./...` shows `no tests to run` everywhere) — if so, the story MUST add tests that satisfy the prefix, not just wire the dedicated step. (2) `VALUE-TYPE STRUCT FIELD SHAPE` — when the canonical conformance test reads a struct field that's a value type (not a pointer), the tes