fd00::1]` shape because url.Parse with a colon-bearing v6 address outside brackets parses the colons as port separators; the runtime test fixtures call this out explicitly. The disallowedSSRFHost helper strips one set of surrounding brackets so it accepts BOTH the URL-extracted (already unbracketed) form AND a literal bracketed form a caller might supply directly. Layered defence is explicit in AGENTS.md: this is the PURE validator layer (no DNS) and a second wall in the HTTP/git client at fetch time is REQUIRED to catch DNS-rebinding (a public name resolving to an internal IP at fetch time). The validator is the first wall; the runtime resolved-IP re-check is a separate story.
