rvices which DO have one), the `assertXxxByteIdentical` MUST NOT compare a version column and the file header MUST call out `updated_at` as the SOLE trigger-managed drift anchor (the BEFORE UPDATE set_updated_at trigger is the load-bearing anchor; a missing organization_id predicate would surface as updated_at drift even when every other column happened to look right). Mandatory test shape (the 8 tests this file lands, adapted from BE-0458): Insert(orgA)DoesNotTouchOrgB (byte-identity over queued + running-with-live-lease + idempotency-collide bystanders), Insert(orgA)DoesNotChangeOrgBRowCount, InsertSameIdempotencyKeyInTwoTenantsBothPersist (positive direction + per-tenant FindByIdempotencyKey round-trip), GetCrossTenantReturnsNotFoundAndDoesNotEcho (typed apierr.NotFound + substring no-leak on idempotency_key/request_id/correlation_id/project_id), FindByIdempotencyKeyCrossTenantDoesNotLeak (returns (zero, false, nil) + zero-value field-by-field no-leak), <StateMutation>CrossTenantLeavesOrgABystandersByteIdentical (the table's single mutating surface attempted by orgB on orgA's id -- Cancel for deployments, Transition(..., cancelled, mut) for jobs -- MUST surface as apierr.NotFound NOT Conflict, because the FOR UPDATE SELECT under (organization_id, id) returns ErrNoRows BEFORE the state-machine validator runs; bystanders include the named target + queued sibling + running sibling carrying a live lease), ListByOrganizationCrossTenantReturnsEmptyAndDoesNotLeakTotal (empty slice + side-effect-free read + per-tenant COUNT(*) invariance), OrganizationDeleteCascadeIsTenantScoped (orgA deletion cascades only to orgA's rows; orgB rows survive byte-identical -- include a row carrying a live lease to anchor lease_owner/lease_deadline/started_at). Always document in the file header what the file DELIBERATELY DELEGATES (composite-FK cross-tenant-parent path pinned by invariants story, closed-set / lifecycle CHECKs / state-machine matrix / lease bookkeeping / claimer pinned by subsystem story, redactor + payload marshalling pinned by internal_test) so a future reader does not mistake the omission for a coverage gap. When the table's worker-side claimer is INTENTIONALLY NOT tenant-scoped (e.g. ClaimNext SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED across all tenants), call it out explicitly in the header rationale. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation story whose table follows the (subsystem-tests + invariants-tests + table-has-no-version-column) shape (e.g. future job_attempts / dokploy_refs if their repos land before their PRD stories).
