mysql/mongo/redis database without re-reading the spec body. (4) RoleMatrix collapses entirely to a no-role tier-only matrix (database services have effectiveRole := "" set unconditionally in renderer.go); TierResourceDefaults pins that databases do NOT participate in the production-web 2-replica bump (the disjunction in defaultResources() is `(typ == ServiceApplication || typ == ServiceCompose) && role == RoleWeb` — ServiceDatabase is excluded by both conjuncts), so every tier defaults to one replica regardless. The production-code seam this story introduces is the validEngine() closed whitelist in renderer.go: BE-0309 ships only EnginePostgres = "postgres"; BE-0311..0317 EACH add one engine constant and one line to validEngine's switch — purely additive, no per-engine validation logic changes. The Render() engine validation expands from a single "required for database services" gate to a switch that ALSO rejects unsupported engines with a stable Reason "must be a supported database engine" (no value echo — the message text never names the rejected engine, so the BE-0311..0317 stories that add engines do NOT need to change the message). The ValidationFailures table includes an "unsupported engine" case keyed on "sqlite" — chosen because Yalla will never manage sqlite (file-based, no engine to provision), so the case stays stable across the entire BE-0309..0317 family even as the whitelist grows. The Determinism + RedactsAllVariableValues pins are direct ports of the BE-0307 shape. database.golden in testdata/renderer/ needs the +yalla.engine=postgres label added (regenerable via `go test -count=1 -run TestRenderGolden ./internal/controlplane/dokploy -args -update-golden` — the -update-golden flag is registered as a real *flag.Bool via init() in internal/testutil/golden.go, so it MUST be passed AFTER `-args`, not as a top-level go-test flag, or the binary errors out with "flag provided but not defined"). The worker-side acceptance criteria (dokploy_refs atomic write, quota reservation-to-conversion, fake Dokploy create/update/deploy/poll/failure/retry/replay) all defer to the later database worker story per the BE-0301 deferral pattern. Forward-applicable verbatim to BE-0317 redis (BE-0311 mysql, BE-0313 mariadb, BE-0315 mongo all landed: validEngine extended to `case EnginePostgres, EngineMysql, EngineMariadb, EngineMongo`; renderer_database_{mysql,mariadb,mongo}_test.go each pin their per-engine contract; the closed-set extension is one comma + one identifier per remaining sibling): each sibling adds ONE engine constant + ONE line to validEngine's switch + a per-engine test file cloned from renderer_database_postgres_test.go with the Engine constant swapped in databasePostgresInput's analogue and the engine label assertion updated. NOT applicable to non-database service types or to subtypes whose discriminator is the Builder or the ServiceType.

